---
description: Keep README.md and AGENTS.md current with Saint Shard
alwaysApply: true
---

For every repository change, review and update README.md and AGENTS.md together with an accurate explanation, including changes to gameplay, assets, saves, configuration, tests, tooling and documentation. Do not substitute timestamp-only or whitespace-only edits for actual documentation. Both files must still quote the four goal sentences from lib/story/goal.ts and the save key saint-shard-3055-v1. lib/docs.test.ts checks that. CI also runs scripts/docs-freshness.mjs against the complete push or pull request range and blocks Test when either document lacks changed content. Identical repository trees need no artificial edits; unavailable comparison history must fail rather than skip. Automated checks enforce content updates; always review their accuracy and completeness before committing or deploying.

Every new scene needs an explicit art decision in qa/media/scene-art.json and accompanying art when its setting, character or major visual moment requires it. Ship needed art with the scene, reuse fitting assets, and record the rationale when text is sufficient. No automatic decisions for future scenes. Follow AGENTS.md and docs/AUTHORING.md; keep art consistent with known outcomes and preserve text-only mode.
